  "response": "A, feeling taken for granted is understandable when an agreed task remains undone, but the dishes alone do not establish that B expected you to handle them. B, an important call can explain forgetting without removing responsibility for the agreement. You could acknowledge the impact and arrange to finish the dishes. A could ask what happened rather than assume an intention. A useful conversation would separate the missed task from what it meant to each of you, then agree on how to communicate when an unexpected interruption affects a shared commitment."
